<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Advance Australia Fair</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1878">1878</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Advance <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> Fair is the national anthem of Australia, written by Peter Dodds McCormick and first performed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-nova-scotia">Sydney</a> in 1878. After being chosen in a national poll in 1977, it was proclaimed the national anthem in 1984, replacing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/god-save-the-king">God Save the Queen</a>, which remained the royal anthem. Its words were changed in 2021 from 'young and free' to 'one and free'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/advance-australia-fair.jpg" alt="Advance Australia Fair" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Dodds McCormick · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Advance_Australia_Fair_(1878).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A separate Australian citizenship was created in 1949, and <b>Advance Australia Fair</b> replaced God Save the Queen as the national anthem in 1984.</blockquote><a href="/empire/commonwealth-of-australia">Commonwealth of Australia · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>The Whitlam government held a competition in 1973 that produced no music and a shortlist of lyrics that critics derided, and then an opinion poll of about 60,000 people that offered only &quot;<b>Advance Australia Fair</b>&quot;, &quot;Waltzing Matilda&quot; and &quot;Song of Australia&quot;.</blockquote><a href="/songs/advance-australia-fair">Advance Australia Fair</a></li><li><blockquote>In the national plebiscite of 1977 it was one of four choices for Australia's national song, with &quot;Waltzing Matilda&quot;, the then anthem &quot;God Save the Queen&quot; and &quot;<b>Advance Australia Fair</b>&quot;.</blockquote><a href="/songs/the-song-of-australia">The Song of Australia</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 1977 plebiscite on a national song it came second with about 28%, behind &quot;<b>Advance Australia Fair</b>&quot;.</blockquote><a href="/songs/waltzing-matilda">Waltzing Matilda</a></li></ul></section>
